<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20555" root="سلم" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْلَمُ</span></b>  [<i>More,</i> and <i>most, safe</i> or <i>secure</i> or <i>free
from evils of any kind</i>]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا أَسْلَمُ مِنْ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا</span> [<i>This is more safe</i> &amp;c. <i>than this</i>]: and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَسْلَمُ</span> [<i>This is the most safe</i> &amp;c.]; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذِهِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السُّلْمَى</span>. (Ham p. 214.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الاسلم</span> [app.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَسْلَمُ</span>] signifies, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الطفى</span> [i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الطَّفْىُ</span>]; <i>The
leaves</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُوص</span>) <i>of the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَوْم</span> [or <i>Theban palm</i>].
(Ibn-Beytár, app. from AHn, cited by De Sacy
in his Chrest. Arabe, 2nd ed., iii. 480.)

